{
  "duration": 72.4,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.12,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.74,
      "end": 2.939,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.5,
      "end": 4.38,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.779,
      "end": 5.579,
      "text": "In this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.199,
      "end": 7.519,
      "text": "we have a ramp that rises"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.0,
      "end": 11.859,
      "text": "seven meters for a horizontal run of seven square root of three meters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.42,
      "end": 15.359,
      "text": "and we need to find the angle that the ramp makes with the ground."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.02,
      "end": 16.42,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.959,
      "end": 18.52,
      "text": "let's visualize the right"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.939,
      "end": 19.559,
      "text": "triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.0,
      "end": 22.539,
      "text": "The vertical rise is the opposite side,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.979,
      "end": 23.119,
      "text": "so"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.6,
      "end": 25.599,
      "text": "opposite equals seven meters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.26,
      "end": 28.5,
      "text": "and the horizontal run is the adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.979,
      "end": 32.819,
      "text": "So adjacent equals seven square root of three meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.459,
      "end": 33.619,
      "text": "Now,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.119,
      "end": 34.36,
      "text": "which"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.7,
      "end": 38.379,
      "text": "trigonometric ratio uses the opposite and adjacent sides?"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.779,
      "end": 39.239,
      "text": "It's ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.799,
      "end": 42.739,
      "text": "So ten theta equals opposite over adjacent."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.259,
      "end": 44.52,
      "text": "Substituting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.02,
      "end": 56.219,
      "text": "ten theta equals seven over seven square root of three. The seven cancels out, giving us ten theta equals one over square root of three."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.799,
      "end": 58.159,
      "text": "Now we know the standard value,"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.759,
      "end": 61.599,
      "text": "ten thirty degrees equals one over square root of three."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.239,
      "end": 62.739,
      "text": "Therefore,"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.359,
      "end": 65.119,
      "text": "theta equals thirty degrees."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.959,
      "end": 70.08,
      "text": "So the angle made by the ramp with the ground is thirty degrees."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.54,
      "end": 72.4,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
